      "text": [
        "4377 - : وَ قَامَ اَلنَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اَللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَ آلِهِ خَطِيباً فَقَالَ \"أَيُّهَا اَلنَّاسُ إِيَّاكُمْ وَ خَضْرَاءَ اَلدِّمَنِ \" قِيلَ يَا رَسُولَ اَللَّهِ وَ مَا خَضْرَاءُ اَلدِّمَنِ قَالَ \"اَلْمَرْأَةُ اَلْحَسْنَاءُ فِي مَنْبِتِ اَلسَّوْءِ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.4377 - The Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) stood up to deliver a sermon and said: \"O people, beware of the green growth in a dung heap.\"\nIt was asked: \"O Messenger of Allah (swt), what is the green growth in a dung heap?\"\nHe (sw) replied: \"A beautiful woman raised in a bad environment.\""
        ]
      }
